9. Validation Rules

Before accepting a new task, the system needs to check whether the information provided by the user is correct.

The following validation rules should be applied:

The task title must not be empty.

The description is optional and can be left blank.

The assignee ID must belong to an existing user.

The due date must follow the YYYY-MM-DD format.

The priority must be either low, medium, or high.

The project ID must identify an existing project.

The user must be authenticated and have permission to create tasks in the selected project.

If the submitted information does not meet these requirements, the server should return an appropriate error response explaining the problem.

10. Conclusion

This API endpoint provides a straightforward way to create tasks within a project management application.

By using the POST method, users can submit the necessary information and receive confirmation when a task is successfully created.

In designing this endpoint, I have considered the importance of authentication, correct data formats, validation, and appropriate HTTP response codes.

These elements help make the API easier to understand, use, and maintain.

